{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1199339-howl-of-death-territory-red-talons-gifts","id":1199339,"title":"Howl of Death + Territory (Red Talons gifts)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-25T03:48:00-07:00","id":1199339,"title":"Howl of Death + Territory (Red Talons gifts)","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> I've been wondering what you all think about using Territory (a rank 3 Red Talon gift) with Howl of Death (a rank 4 Red Talon gift).<br /> <br /> Howl of Death requires clear vision of the target and the target being within appropriate distance to hear the howl. So, assuming the Red Talon is physically close enough for the target to heal the howl but too far to have proper sight of it, and it just so happens to be within a marked area. Territory will allow the Talon to view the target very clearly, which answers 1 part of the Howl of Death requirements while also being close enough to hear the howl, which answers the second requirement.<br /> <br /> What do you all think? I mean, would you allow this to be used?<br /> <br /> I personally think it is appropriate of such high rank gifts and would have no problem allowing it (as I see no other problem other than it being very powerful at certain scenarios).<br /> <br /> Thank you,<br /> TataCavalier","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23978-tatacavalier","name":"TataCavalier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T13:47:16-07:00","id":1199465,"title":"","content":"I would allow it, but if they didn't get three successes on the Territory roll I would increase the difficulty on HoD. I would say +1 for each success not achieved, showing the strain of trying to remain focused on one gift while channeling the other. They would also have to stop pursuit, if they are chasing, for 2 rounds (1 for the activation of each gift).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}